            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0683" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/462: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-02T17:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1919, 5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 3, 1.24
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3008. My telegram number 2076 May 7th, 3 p.m. Cabrera now states that nothing can
                    be done in regard to provisional permits to drill until after return of General
                    Calles, the Secretary of Industry and Commerce, about June 20th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
